(Title) Tj
T*
(Efficacy of Integrated Digital Care Management in Reducing Pruritis and Improving Clinical) Tj
T*
(Outcomes in Adults With Atopic Dermatitis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Itch represents the cardinal symptom driving disability in atopic dermatitis, yet) Tj
T*
(conventional episodic care often inadequately addresses this burden. We randomly assigned) Tj
T*
(98 participants \(mean age 42 years, 45% female\) to receive either integrated online care) Tj
T*
(coordination \(n=49\) or standard care \(n=49\). At 12-week assessment, the coordinated-care) Tj
T*
(group demonstrated clinically meaningful reductions in itch severity compared with) Tj
T*
(controls \(mean difference 2.9 points on 10-point scale, p<0.001\). Disease severity scores) Tj
T*
(measuring extent and intensity of skin involvement improved significantly in the) Tj
T*
(intervention arm \(p<0.001\). Sleep quality measurements showed greater improvement in the) Tj
T*
(online-care group \(mean difference 1.8 points, p=0.03\). Dermatitis-related quality-of-life) Tj
T*
(scores increased substantially in the intervention group \(p<0.001\). No serious adverse) Tj
T*
(events were documented. Participant satisfaction with care delivery was high in both) Tj
T*
(groups, though the online-care participants reported preferring the coordinated approach) Tj
T*
(for future management.) Tj
ET
